  {
   "id": "translate",
   "h2": "Translating the imperfect",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "facts": [
      "Find the <em>-ba-</em>, or <em>er-</em> in <em>sum</em>, then the person ending.",
      "Something going on: \"was ...ing\" or \"were ...ing\". <em>servi laborabant</em>, \"the slaves were working\".",
      "A habit: \"used to ...\". <em>semper laborabant</em>, \"they always used to work\".",
      "<em>erat</em> is \"he was\", \"she was\" or \"there was\"; <em>erant</em> is \"they were\" or \"there were\"."
     ]
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "nautae diu naviga<u class=\"c\">ba</u><u class=\"v\">nt</u>.",
      "en": "The sailors <b>were sailing</b> for a long time."
     }
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "domina Romae habita<u class=\"c\">ba</u><u class=\"v\">t</u>.",
      "en": "The mistress <b>used to live</b> in Rome."
     }
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "servi in foro <u class=\"c\">era</u><u class=\"v\">nt</u>.",
      "en": "The slaves <b>were</b> in the forum.",
      "note": "<em>erant</em> is the imperfect of <em>sum</em>: \"they were\"."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "watch",
   "h2": "Watch out",
   "exam": true,
   "label": "Common mistakes",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "facts": [
      "<em>-bam</em> is \"I\": <em>portabam</em>, \"I was carrying\". \"He was carrying\" is <em>portabat</em>.",
      "<em>-bat</em> is one person, <em>-bant</em> more than one: check the last letters, as in the present.",
      "<em>erat</em> is \"he was\"; <em>est</em> is \"he is\". The two look alike.",
      "The imperfect is past. \"Is carrying\" is the present; <em>portabat</em> is \"was carrying\"."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
